# How to cite EMIR (Citation File Format 1.2.0, https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# The authors follow the copyright line of LICENSE (MIT). `version` follows
# emir/__init__.py (tests/test_community_files.py).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EMIR in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EMIR: EM / IR-drop screening of extracted analog layout"
abstract: >-
  EMIR screens extracted analog layout for electromigration and IR drop: a DSPF
  (or a GDS layout) and simulated or DC currents give per-segment EM ratios
  (average, rms, peak) against the process limits, the IR drop, HTML reports and
  Virtuoso and KLayout viewers. It is built to be driven by AI agents, with JSON
  output, stable error codes and a recommended next command. A screening tool,
  not sign-off; a research project, provided as is, with no warranty or
  guarantee of accuracy.
authors:
  - given-names: Vijay
    family-names: Gupta
  - name: "EMIR contributors"
version: 1.1.0.dev0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/skycadeda/emir"
url: "https://skycadeda.github.io/emir/"
keywords:
  - electromigration
  - IR drop
  - EDA
  - analog layout
  - DSPF
  - AI agents
